(i) The jurisdictional Executive Engineer along with the concerned officer shall cause a inspection of the property, carry out a survey of the same, if necessary, by taking assistance of the jurisdictional ADLR, mark the extent of the land which is proposed to be used in the presence of the land owners to quantify the extent of the land used on the basis of the marking made above, a copy of the Survey sketch to be signed by all such officers clearly denoting their designation and identifying factors and made Sri K S Junjappa vs The State Of Karnataka on 18 December, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/176677759/
6 part of the file;
- 12 - NC: 2023:KHC:46518 (ii) Valuation of the land used for public purpose by the Corporation including for widening of the road or laying of new road or any other public purpose, to be made and valuation sheet enclosed in the file signed by the concerned officers clearly denoting their designation and identifying factors;
(iii) To ascertain if there are any buildings which are located in the said property, obtain copies of the plan sanctioned relating to the same and certify the extent of building which would be required to be demolished for the aforesaid public purpose, the age of the building and valuation of the building to be annexed to the said report along with the photographs of the said building;
(iv) The geographical location of the building would be marked by longitude and latitude basis by taking necessary photographs by using an - 13 - NC: 2023:KHC:46518 application like Dishaank which has been created by the Revenue Department;
(v) Prepare a superimposed sketch of the property of the landloser in conjunction with the RMP or CDP applicable thereto and make it part of the report.
(vi) Once the above proceedings are completed and the land of the landloser is identified for the use of BBMP, a Relinquishment Deed to be executed by the land owner in favour of BBMP which shall be registered with a sketch attached to the said document detailing out the measurement of the land as well as the building, if any and other documents mentioned above;
(vii) On such relinquishment being executed, BBMP to, within 30 days from the date of the relinquishment deed, forward a recommendation to the BDA or such other local - 14 - NC: 2023:KHC:46518 planning authority having jurisdiction for issuance of necessary DRC;
(viii) The planning authority to consider such recommendation and issue DRC within a period of 15 days of such recommendation being received in terms of the applicable rules.

